https://github.com/alchaincyf/nuwa-skill/blob/7812110bf7e5a2b01b6aa5a738568044121bbfa2/references/skill-template.md

## 2. Main slide

TIME 0:55. Our answer is yes: Nuwa's methodology is valuable as a design pattern for authoring evidence-backed reasoning capabilities in AI4Research. It shows how to research expert reasoning, extract reusable rules with source support and failure conditions, and convert them into concrete investigation steps. We can imitate that method in hypothesis generation, experiment design and evaluation, then extend the CC factory with a person-plus-trait interface. The table-driven explanation that follows shows the research step before its extracted products. Hypothesis work can preserve competing explanations, experiment design can turn assumptions into evidence questions, and evaluation can retain counterexamples. This is a positive assessment of the methodology's design utility. Actual task-quality gains still need a matched experiment, and the source, validation and persona-authority pitfalls need stronger checks.

