## 4. Main slide

TIME 1:00. A mental model is a reusable lens, while a decision rule tells the agent what to do in a particular situation. Nuwa keeps three to seven models. Each must recur across at least two domains, generate judgments on new questions, and distinguish the person's perspective from generic advice. A qualifying model needs supporting scenes, an application and a limitation. Decision heuristics are concrete if-then rules, typically five to ten, with case evidence. The Karpathy example links understanding through construction to rebuilding a minimal core, and contains a data-inspection-before-training rule. We paraphrase the repository's extracted skill here, not independently verified personal statements. Nuwa also records tensions and derives factual research directions from the models. AI4R could imitate this separation of a rationale, an executable step, its evidence requirements and its failure conditions. These qualitative filters select useful candidates; they do not validate scientific correctness.

