## 7. Main slide

TIME 1:00. The factory can be understood as one capability-production system with three entry interfaces. First, a gap observed during a run supplies the missing responsibility, task context and failure evidence; diagnosis turns it into a requirement brief. Second, a paper, repository and data supply an existing method to reproduce and adapt. Third, a person's name plus a target trait, such as Karpathy and reliability review, supplies a research intent. That route discovers and prepares relevant sources, then extracts supported models and rules. A name and desired trait alone are not enough to establish a capability. The three routes share a candidate contract, implementation and evidence package, then independent qualification and the existing admission gate. They do not share identical authoring work. Source preparation is separately authorized and pinned before offline build work. A runtime gap does not authorize automatic promotion either. This is a proposed M2 interface direction, starting with flat stages and bounded authoring agents; it does not claim three implemented entry points today.

SOURCES
https://github.com/alchaincyf/nuwa-skill/blob/7812110bf7e5a2b01b6aa5a738568044121bbfa2/SKILL.md
