## 8. Main slide

TIME 0:50. Start with one source-rich expert corpus and one bounded responsibility, such as reviewing an agent benchmark. Use Nuwa's extraction method to draft a neutral, source-linked review procedure. Pin the procedure and cutoff, and require outputs to distinguish source-supported rules, framework inference and current task evidence. Compare it against a plain reviewer and a length-matched generic review checklist. All arms get the same expert-source excerpts and task evidence, model, tools and runtime budget. Freeze new tasks and scoring before generation, and use blinded human judgment. Measure supported useful objections, missed failures, calibration and cost. Record authoring cost separately. Retain the procedure only if it improves real review behavior beyond the generic checklist. A persona-voice ablation can follow later if relevant.

SOURCES
https://github.com/alchaincyf/nuwa-skill/blob/7812110bf7e5a2b01b6aa5a738568044121bbfa2/SKILL.md
